uadratic term is $a=2,$ the expression $2{y}^{2}-8y+26$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-8y+26 & =a(y-{y}_{1})(y-{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283556 13194139534327 true] [17592186283555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283557 13194139534327 true] [17592186283555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283558 13194139534327 true] [17592186283555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283559 13194139534327 true] [17592186283555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283560 13194139534327 true] [17592186283555 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534327 true] [17592186283555 1041 "selection" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283555 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283557 13194139534327 true] [17592186283555 1110 #uuid "3f9a4def-79fc-56b9-a709-e1e9a9793b19" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283556 1034 "(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i}))" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283556 1111 #uuid "d13abf36-6279-5f10-9364-c9263073b372" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283557 1034 "2(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i}))" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283557 1111 #uuid "6e55e4c0-4cb2-5c6d-af8b-15ba49b941bd" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283558 1034 "2(y-(1+3\\text{i}))(y-(1-3\\text{i}))" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283558 1111 #uuid "6392ad34-87de-5037-8eff-f93cd57e2275" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283559 1034 "(y-(1+3\\text{i}))(y-(1-3\\text{i}))" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283559 1111 #uuid "f359569e-3de1-51a8-8beb-732c0fd896d7" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283560 1034 "2(y-(2+\\text{i}))(y-(2-\\text{i}))" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283560 1111 #uuid "624a5063-a5dd-557f-86f8-b0904b2d9bbf" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283561 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283562 13194139534327 true] [17592186283561 1089 "q-46588" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283561 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534327 true] [17592186283561 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $P(y)$ has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3.$ Find $P(y).$" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283561 1113 #uuid "18d53b8b-4f6d-534c-9744-bb5236603b18" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283561 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})^{2} & =3{(y-3)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(y-3)}^{2} & =3({y}^{2}-6y+9) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-18y+27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(y)=3{y}^{2}-18y+27.$" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283562 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283563 13194139534327 true] [17592186283562 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283564 13194139534327 true] [17592186283562 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283565 13194139534327 true] [17592186283562 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283566 13194139534327 true] [17592186283562 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283567 13194139534327 true] [17592186283562 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534327 true] [17592186283562 1041 "selection" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283562 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283566 13194139534327 true] [17592186283562 1110 #uuid "f74d1c05-d8a9-5a2d-811c-febb1ad6cb72" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283563 1034 "3{y}^{2}-24y+27" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283563 1111 #uuid "56ad7dde-8db0-5afb-9f99-61bb479a2dd9" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283564 1034 "3{y}^{2}-18y-27" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283564 1111 #uuid "afaee32b-8ff0-53f1-9262-24b38997e006" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283565 1034 "3{y}^{2}-9y-27" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283565 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283565 1111 #uuid "42632239-8018-56ee-907e-78d2d1fe1b1f" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283566 1034 "3{y}^{2}-18y+27" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283566 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283566 1111 #uuid "1c4fb670-5118-5c11-9a3b-73af922ef8ac" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283567 1034 "3{y}^{2}-9y+27" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283567 1111 #uuid "6ade4beb-68f9-5374-9c02-810b957b08db" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283568 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283569 13194139534327 true] [17592186283568 1089 "q-46657" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283568 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534327 true] [17592186283568 1100 "Which of the following is a factor of ${u}^{2}-4u+40?$" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283568 1113 #uuid "cc2e6627-c76f-5b42-ba0e-7e3f345cefbd" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283568 1145 "First, we let $f(u)={u}^{2}-4u+40.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(u)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(u) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2}-4u+40 & =0 \\\\ ({u}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot u+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2}+40 & =0 \\\\ (u-2)^{2}-4+40 & =0 \\\\ (u-2)^{2}+36 & =0 \\\\ (u-2)^{2} & =-36 \\\\ (u-2)^{2} & =36{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (u-2)^{2} & =(6\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ u-2 & =\\pm 6\\text{i} \\\\ u & =2\\pm 6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our quadratic equation has roots ${u}_{1}=2+6\\text{i}$ and ${u}_{2}=2-6\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression ${u}^{2}-4u+40$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-4u+40 & =a(u-{u}_{1})(u-{u}_{2}) \\\\  & =(u-(2+6\\text{i}))(u-(2-6\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, among the given options, only $u-(2-6\\text{i})$ is a factor of ${u}^{2}-4u+40.$" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283570 13194139534327 true] [17592186283569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283571 13194139534327 true] [17592186283569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283572 13194139534327 true] [17592186283569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283573 13194139534327 true] [17592186283569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283574 13194139534327 true] [17592186283569 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534327 true] [17592186283569 1041 "selection" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283569 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283573 13194139534327 true] [17592186283569 1110 #uuid "a678b094-63b7-53be-b9fb-b9d46527f020" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283570 1034 "u-(1-4\\text{i})" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283570 1111 #uuid "72740904-b7e4-5235-90bf-c1349124d852" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283571 1034 "u-(-2-6\\text{i})" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283571 1111 #uuid "67fd16aa-0801-532e-9f9b-427d3210306f" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283572 1034 "u-(3-4\\text{i})" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283572 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283572 1111 #uuid "abd4deea-095a-571d-bbfb-d90fc18b28db" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283573 1034 "u-(2-6\\text{i})" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283573 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283573 1111 #uuid "a942ade8-acc0-5f2b-90b3-eaa7ea4a90ea" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283574 1034 "u+(1+4\\text{i})" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283574 1111 #uuid "973f6954-dc4a-53c5-a4bc-6059846cd542" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283575 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283576 13194139534327 true] [17592186283575 1089 "q-46669" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283575 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534327 true] [17592186283575 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $f(v)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${v}_{1}=3+4\\text{i}$ and ${v}_{2}=3-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $f(v).$" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283575 1113 #uuid "b39aa3d6-40fa-5b31-9981-0e48c9722e25" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283575 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${v}_{1}=3+4\\text{i}$ and ${v}_{2}=3-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(v-{v}_{1})(v-{v}_{2}) & =2(v-(3+4\\text{i}))(v-(3-4\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(v-(3+4\\text{i}))(v-(3-4\\text{i})) & =2({v}^{2}-(3+4\\text{i})v-(3-4\\text{i})v+(3+4\\text{i})(3-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2({v}^{2}-(3+4\\text{i}+3-4\\text{i})v+({3}^{2}-{4}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2})) \\\\  & =2({v}^{2}-6v+(9+16)) \\\\  & =2{v}^{2}-12v+50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(v)=2{v}^{2}-12v+50.$" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283577 13194139534327 true] [17592186283576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283578 13194139534327 true] [17592186283576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283579 13194139534327 true] [17592186283576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283580 13194139534327 true] [17592186283576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283581 13194139534327 true] [17592186283576 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534327 true] [17592186283576 1041 "selection" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283576 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283577 13194139534327 true] [17592186283576 1110 #uuid "3f4390f7-86ba-51b5-a3a1-72b7af3f8784" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283577 1034 "2{v}^{2}-12v+50" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283577 1111 #uuid "a76d1eff-832f-53c0-81ab-a3e5dca329ba" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283578 1034 "2{v}^{2}+6v+25" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283578 1111 #uuid "d79ae51b-9fe9-5cb3-95f4-378d4d53ae83" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283579 1034 "2{v}^{2}+8v-14" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283579 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534327 true] [17592186283579 1111 #uuid "f8c0854c-a5a8-580e-81bc-97ad7d63f4f8" 13194139534327 true] [17592186283580 1034 "2{v}^{2}-16v-14" 131941395